          },
          "message": "feat: preserve force-push commits on PRs through `git gc` (#15162)\n\nImplements #8279.\n\nWhenever a force push occurs on an open PR (via branch or AGit), an additional reference is created in the base git in the form of `refs/pull/N/comment/M/{old,new}`.  `N` is the pull request index, `M` is the internal ID of the timeline comment on the PR, and `old` or `new` are used for either the commit previous to the force push, or the commit after the force push.  The new references are read-only and cannot be modified or deleted by external `git push` operations.  The references are removed if the pull request is deleted (but not if the pull request is closed).\n\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/15162\nReviewed-by: Andreas Ahlenstorf <redacted@example.invalid>\n",
          "tree": {
            "url": "https://codeberg.org/api/v1/repos/forgejo/forgejo/git/trees/6c2b8b9d726a44abbaf7bc07d293cb10e93829a7",
